<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the iOS app (required since 2024 for required-reason
  APIs). Rewritten for 1.1 (2026-09-29); second pass the same day.

  Accessed APIs (required reasons):
    - UserDefaults, CA92.1: the app reading its own preferences (migration
      flags, AppStorage-backed setup choices). 1C8F.1 (added 2026-09-23,
      Block): `BlockKit/BlockStore.swift` reading and writing the App Group
      (`group.com.lockout.meditate808`) this app shares with its three Block
      extensions (Monitor, Shield, ShieldAction): the blockers, passes and
      holds Screen Time has to see across processes. The Block code ships in
      the binary even while `blockInRelease` is off. Nothing in the App Group
      leaves the phone; see BlockKit's own header.
    - File timestamp, C617.1 (added 2026-09-29): the store-file dates
      `Shared/Persistence.swift` reads when it moves the SwiftData stores out
      of the App Group container (files inside the app's own and the group's
      container only), and the file dates PostHog's SDK reads on its own
      event queue in the app container.
    - System boot time, 35F9.1 (added 2026-09-29): PostHog's SDK measures
      elapsed time between events with it. Never sent off the device as a
      boot time.

  Collected data, as 1.1 ships (Friends ON with profiles only and no posts,
  Block ON, Shop ON, Otto chat OFF; Block sends nothing off the device and
  the Shop's events are Product Interaction, so neither adds a type). Apple's "collect" means sent off the
  device where we or a third party can read it. Each type appears ONCE, so
  where two uses share a type the entry carries the stronger linkage and
  every purpose. Nothing is tracking.

  PostHog analytics (`Coherence/Analytics/Analytics.swift`, Release only).
  ALL LINKED since 2026-09-29: every event from an install carries the same
  random distinct_id, and Apple counts data tied to a pseudonymous
  identifier as linked to the user. It is never tied to a name, email,
  Apple ID or Friends username. Named events only: screen views, session
  replay, element-interaction (rage-click) autocapture, surveys and push
  capture are all off.
    - Product Interaction: named behavioral events, with coarse bands
      (session length, streak) where an event has them. Linked. Analytics.
    - Purchase History: plan picked, purchase, trial, restore, entitlement
      lost, and the `is_subscriber` / `plan` person properties. No payment
      details, so Financial Info stays off. Linked. Analytics.
    - Coarse Location: PostHog derives country, region and city from the IP
      address of every request (GeoIP), and the founders read it in the
      Google Sheet copy (`tools/posthog_sheet.gs`). Linked. Analytics.
    - Other Usage Data: the device and app metadata the SDK attaches to every
      event (iPhone model, iOS version, app version and build, TestFlight or
      not, language, time zone, screen size, Wi-Fi or cellular), the
      install, update, open and close lifecycle events, and the
      `has_paired_watch` / `app_flow` person properties. Linked. Analytics.
    - User ID: the random install-scoped distinct_id (a UUID in the SDK's
      own storage, never the IDFA or identifierForVendor), reset on sign-out
      and account deletion. Shares the type with the Friends @username
      below, so the single entry carries both purposes.
  No Diagnostics entry: PostHog's bundled crash-reporter manifest declares
  crash data, but crash capture is off in `Analytics.swift`
  (`errorTrackingConfig.autoCapture = false`), so nothing is collected.

  Friends (public CloudKit database of our own container, which we can
  read, so by Apple's definition collected; all LINKED, a profile is the
  person; App Functionality):
    - User ID: the @username, chosen and public.
    - Name: the display name on a profile.
    - Photos or Videos: the optional profile photo. (Session photos and
      videos stay in the user's PRIVATE iCloud and are not collected.)
    - Other Data Types: the practice summary on the profile (sessions and
      minutes in the last 7 days, streak, total sessions, last session
      date), the first-session and created dates, and the friend edges and
      blocks the person writes. Derived from session dates and lengths,
      never from the body.
    - Other User Content: the reason text on a report, which is stored in
      the public database and sent to the reports web app
      (`ReportClient`, `tools/community-reports.gs`).

  Earlier waitlist (`WaitlistClient`): the no-Watch waitlist screen is cut,
  but an email can still reach the waitlist sheet two ways: a saved
  onboarding record from an older version that held one
  (`OnboardingView`, `WaitlistClient.submit`), and a queued sign-up that
  flushes on launch (`WaitlistClient.flush`).
    - Email Address: LINKED, Developer's Advertising or Marketing.

  What is deliberately NOT collected, and must never appear here: health and
  fitness data. Heart rate, breathing, stillness, scores, and every value
  derived from them stay on device (HealthKit data may not be disclosed to
  third parties, guideline 5.1.3). No 1.1 analytics event carries one, and a
  Friends profile never does. The private CloudKit database (account,
  sessions, notes, session photos) is the user's own and is not collected:
  we cannot read it. Nothing Block or Screen Time learns ever leaves the
  phone (Apple's Family Controls terms).

  The App Privacy labels in App Store Connect must match this file. Change
  the manifest, PRIVACY_POLICY.md and the labels together, always.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeProductInteraction</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurchaseHistory</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeCoarseLocation</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUsageData</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePhotosorVideos</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUserContent</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeDeveloperAdvertising</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
